this run shows a group holding these villages as of 2026. Assessed as state-held with armed-group raiding; recent reporting could not be checked.","unit":"CD6303-punia","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"},{"entity_id":"raia-mutomboki","role":"raiding"}]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Punia centre (Kangina), seat of Punia territory","evidence":"Territorial capital with state administration, police commissariat and FARDC presence; no armed group is known to hold or tax the town. Not verified with recent reporting because web research was blocked.","unit":"CD6303-punia","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-anr","role":"present"},{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[163]}],"sources":{"163":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punia_Territory","title":"Punia Territory","publisher":"Wikipedia"}},"units":{"CD6303-punia":"Punia territory (northeastern Maniema) lies west of the North/South Kivu frontlines and has no recent report, available to this run, of an armed group holding a town or secteur. Punia centre (Kangina) is the territorial administrative seat with PNC, ANR and an FARDC detachment and is assessed as police-held. The rural Punia and Ferekeni secteurs, including the Ferekeni mission centre, are assessed as under default state (PNC/administration) presence. The eastern gold-mining fringe (Kasese, Kibeleketa, Kyolo health areas) borders Lubutu, Walikale and Shabunda, where Raia Mutomboki and other Mai-Mai/Wazalendo groups operate; it has historically seen incursions and armed-group activity around mining sites, so state control there is weaker and confidence low. Web research could not be performed for this unit (search budget exhausted, news and wiki sites egress-blocked), so all zones rest on default state presence or inference from background knowledge."}}